==============================================================================
NN-2  The caustic condition: WHEN does the proper-time/phase saddle go CUBIC?
==============================================================================

[NN-2a] Free action: the sinh^-2 kernel as a saddle problem.
   omega_free(k) = c_chi k :  omega'(k) = c_chi , omega''(k) = 0
   -> NO inflection (omega''=0 nowhere except trivially). No coalescing saddle. QUADRATIC.

[NN-2b] The cubic/caustic condition stated as an operator requirement.
   Need a dispersion (in-medium) omega^2(k) whose phase/group structure develops a
   STATIONARY INFLECTION at the edge: a k* with  d(omega)/dk = v_edge  and
   d^2(omega)/dk^2 = 0  SIMULTANEOUSLY  (two saddles merge). Generic monotone
   dispersions do NOT have this; it requires a TUNED non-monotonic dispersion -- a
   roton-like minimum / inflection in omega(k), i.e. a HIGHER-DERIVATIVE kinetic term.

