==============================================================================
NN-4  The discriminating question: can the EDGE b->c_chi BE the caustic? (MM test)
==============================================================================

[NN-4a] The b-pole is a PARAMETER pole (amplitude), not a saddle coalescence.
   amplitude 1/(c_chi^2-b^2): pole order in (c_chi-b) = 0 (simple in c_chi^2-b^2)
   -> density ~ 1/u, d ln rho/d ln u = -1 (MM's machine -1.000000). A SIMPLE POLE EDGE.
   This coalescence CANNOT be the Airy turning point: it is in the wrong variable.

[NN-4b] So an Airy edge needs a coalescing saddle in tau/k that the FREE op LACKS.
   massless c k: omega''(k) = 0; inflection roots (real,finite) = []
   massive sqrt(c^2k^2+m^2): omega''(k) = c**2*m**2/(c**2*k**2 + m**2)**(3/2); inflection roots (real,finite) = []
   => NO free/massive dispersion has an inflection. NO fold. MM holds: free = non-Airy.

==============================================================================
NN-5  NAME THE OPERATOR: the exact term that promotes quadratic -> cubic
==============================================================================
[NN-5a] omega=sqrt(c0^2 k^2 + alpha k^4): omega''=0 real roots: none (convex up)
[NN-5b] roton omega=sqrt(k^2 - k^4 + 0.1 k^6): omega''=0 (inflection) near k* = [3.29] -> FOLD EXISTS. This dispersion CAN host an Airy turning point.

[NN-5c] The pump term, named precisely:
   The active pump must add a SIGN-INDEFINITE HIGHER-DERIVATIVE kinetic operator to Psi
   that bends the in-medium dispersion non-monotonically (roton-type): concretely a
   term  -alpha (partial_i chi)(partial^2)(partial^i chi)  [a k^4 with the bending sign]
   stabilized by +beta k^6, TUNED so that at the edge frequency the dominant worldline
   saddle sits exactly at the dispersion's INFLECTION (omega''(k*)=0, omega'''(k*)!=0).
   This is the caustic/fold condition. It is the in-medium DISPERSION modification that
   EE-3.2's Bogoliubov lemma already demanded (a dynamics modifier, not a state filler),
   now pinned to its exact analytic shape: a roton inflection coincident with the edge.

[NN-5d] What the FREE operator lacks (the MM gap, stated exactly):
   Free/massive Psi: omega''(k) has NO real finite zero (NN-4b) -> only Gaussian saddles
   -> Watson/Rayleigh-Jeans simple-pole edge, slope -1. The pump must supply the k^4/k^6
   curvature that creates an isolated dispersion INFLECTION; a generic turning point is
   NOT already present (MM), so the fold must be MANUFACTURED by the higher-derivative
   term AND tuned to coincide with the edge. Untuned k^4 -> generic fold at wrong place;
   the edge-coincidence (omega''(k*)=0 AT the b->c_chi resonance) is the extra condition.

